    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Boyington comes for his adult preventive visit, four weeks after his three-month recovery review. The back strain from earlier this month settled within ten days with walking, heat, and a few days of ibuprofen, and he is back to his usual activity. In the past month he drank on one occasion, two beers at a friend&apos;s barbecue, and stopped there; he has had no heavy-drinking day since July. He continues his veteran recovery peer group most weeks. Nightmares are infrequent and he sleeps about six and a half hours. He has had no thoughts of suicide and keeps his safety plan current. He has had no emergency visits or hospital stays. He takes no regular medicines or supplements. He completed the health risk assessment before the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Adult preventive visit, age 44, established patient</td></tr><tr><td>Recent illness</td><td>Lumbar strain earlier this month, resolved</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol</td><td>One occasion of two beers in the past month; AUDIT-C 1</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Alcohol use disorder in early recovery and PTSD after a completed course of prolonged exposure, both improved</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>No suicidal thoughts; safety plan current</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>None regularly; no supplements</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good, and better than in the summer</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Stable housing; support from family, veteran peers, and his recovery group; work stress manageable</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol and drugs</td><td>One drinking occasion in the past month, two beers; no cannabis or other nonprescribed drug use</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>No current tobacco or nicotine use</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Brisk walking 30 minutes on most days; back exercises since the strain</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Regular meals; eats out several times a week; drinks more water and coffee in place of alcohol</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About six and a half hours; occasional nightmares</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent in all basic and instrumental activities of daily living</td></tr><tr><td>Home and personal safety</td><td>Smoke detectors working; wears a seat belt; does not drive after drinking; medicines and any firearms stored locked, as in his safety plan; feels safe at home</td></tr><tr><td>Vision, hearing, and dental</td><td>No vision or hearing concerns; dental cleaning more than a year ago</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

