    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a written prevention plan given. Depression, drug use, and tobacco screens are negative. Blood pressure 124/78 mmHg is normal and has fallen from 134/86 at intake as his drinking fell. [S]<list><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Alcohol use disorder in early recovery (F10.20)</content>. AUDIT-C 1, with no heavy-drinking day since July. Alcohol use disorder is a risk indication for pneumococcal vaccination at his age. The baseline liver tests missed at intake are ordered today. [S]<list><item>Continue the recovery peer group and relapse plan.</item><item>Hepatic panel and GGT ordered today with the preventive blood tests.</item><item>Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine given today.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Post-traumatic stress disorder, improved after prolonged exposure (F43.10)</content>. Nightmares infrequent; no suicidal thoughts. Safety plan current. [S]<list><item>PCL-5 at the recovery check-in in about two months; booster session with Dr. Lee on request.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acute lumbar muscle strain (S39.012A)</content>. Resolved within ten days without imaging or prescription medicines. [S]<list><item>Continue the back exercises and safe lifting.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 score 2 with item 9 scored 0; consistent with his safety assessment</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Known alcohol use disorder followed in his recovery care; AUDIT-C 1 today</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy drug use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No nonprescribed drug use</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No current tobacco or nicotine use</td></tr><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>124/78 mmHg; recheck at each visit</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Age 35 to 70 with overweight (BMI 27.0); HbA1c ordered</td></tr><tr><td>Cholesterol and cardiovascular risk assessment</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Lipid panel ordered to calculate his ten-year cardiovascular risk for the statin decision</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time antigen and antibody test, with his consent; no prior result on record</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time antibody test with reflex RNA, with his consent</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time triple panel; hepatitis B vaccination will be offered if he is not immune</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>This season&apos;s vaccine given today</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20 given today because alcohol use disorder is a risk indication at his age; no further pneumococcal doses needed</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus booster</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap about six years ago; next booster due in about three and a half years</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>Discussed; he plans to get this season&apos;s vaccine at his pharmacy</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Due</td><td>Starts at 45, which he reaches in December. Options were discussed today; he leans toward colonoscopy and will decide at his next visit</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer, abdominal aortic aneurysm, and prostate cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not recommended at his age</td></tr><tr><td>Dental care</td><td>Due</td><td>More than a year since his last cleaning; he will book one</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, 2026-2027 season; Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine (PCV20) [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Substance Use Disorders (2021); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Results of the hepatic panel, GGT, HbA1c, lipid panel, and HIV, hepatitis C, and hepatitis B tests will be sent when available, with a statin discussion if his cardiovascular risk calls for one. Recovery check-in with AUDIT-C, PCL-5, and PHQ-9 in about two months. Next preventive visit in one year. Call or use the crisis line, 988 then 1, at any time. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
